/-!
# Two movers: ALL pairs of positive disparities, all 37 frozen sets (GENERATED by `s2below_gen_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-23.  New file.  For each frozen set of `Sdisp2` (least reading `a`) and ANY two positive mover disparities `d1, d2` (no further hypothesis, no upper
bound): the cascade from `1/(8 min(a, d1, d2))` (the least disparity) reaches a fixed point, every fixed point is the first lonely instant `T`, and `T` exists.
Cases: `min d1 d2 ≤ a` is `S2Below_All` (`landing_twoMoverBelow_*`); both above `a` is `S2Clean_All` (12 clean sets) or `S2Later_All` (25 other sets), whose start
`1/(8a)` equals `1/(8 min(a, d1, d2))` there.  Grades: [L]; [PROVISIONAL: covering] and [PROVISIONAL: counting tool] by inheritance.  Not proved: the cascade's path;
which frozen piece holds the landing as a closed formula (only [OBS]).
-/

